<h3 class=3D"anchor anchorWithStickyNavbar_LWe7" id=3D"slurm-environment-va=
riables">Slurm Environment Variables<a href=3D"https://hyak.uw.edu/docs/com=
pute/scheduling-jobs#slurm-environment-variables" class=3D"hash-link" aria-=
label=3D"Direct link to Slurm Environment Variables" title=3D"Direct link t=
o Slurm Environment Variables">=E2=80=8B</a></h3>
<p>When a job scheduled by Slurm begins, it needs to about how it was sched=
uled, what its working directory is, who submitted the job, the number of n=
odes and cores allocated to it, etc.  This information is passed to Slurm v=
ia environment variables.  Additionally, these environment variables are al=
so used as default values by programs like <code>mpirun</code>.  To view a =
node's Slurm environment variables, use <code>export | grep SLURM</code>.
A comprehensive list of the environment variables Slurm sets for each job c=
an be found at the end of the <a href=3D"https://slurm.schedmd.com/sbatch.h=
tml" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer"><strong><code>sbatch</co=
de> man page</strong></a>.</p>
<h2 class=3D"anchor anchorWithStickyNavbar_LWe7" id=3D"batch-jobs">Batch Jo=
