<h3 class=3D"anchor anchorWithStickyNavbar_LWe7" id=3D"multiple-node-batch-=
jobs">Multiple Node Batch Jobs<a href=3D"https://hyak.uw.edu/docs/compute/s=
cheduling-jobs#multiple-node-batch-jobs" class=3D"hash-link" aria-label=3D"=
Direct link to Multiple Node Batch Jobs" title=3D"Direct link to Multiple N=
ode Batch Jobs">=E2=80=8B</a></h3>
<p>If your batch job is using multiple nodes, your program should also know=
 how to use all the nodes (e.g. your program is an MPI program).</p>
<p>The value given for <code>--nodes</code> should be less than or equal to=
 the total number of nodes owned by your group unless you are running in th=
e <code>ckpt</code> partition.</p>
<p>The value given for <code>--ntasks-per-node</code> can be up to the numb=
er of CPUs your group has available, and CPUs exceeding the groups resource=
s can be requested per job using the checkpoint partitions (<code>ckpt</cod=
e>, <code>ckpt-all</code>, or <code>ckpt-g2</code>). The <code>hyakalloc</c=
ode> command can be used to see the number of CPUs or GPUs that can be requ=
ested under your account/s. In the case you want to use an entire node, the=
 number of CPUs or cores per node varies based on the hardware model, but s=
ome common partitions are the <code>compute</code> partition which have <co=
de>40</code> cores and the <code>cpu-g2</code> and <code>cpu-g2-mem2x</code=
> partitions which have <code>192</code> cores. For example, the below woul=
d request 4 complete nodes from a <code>compute</code> partition.</p>
<div class=3D"language-shell codeBlockContainer_APcc theme-code-block" styl=
e=3D"--prism-color: #bfc7d5; --prism-background-color: #292d3e;"><div class=
=3D"codeBlockContent_m3Ux"><pre tabindex=3D"0" class=3D"prism-code language=
-shell codeBlock_qGQc thin-scrollbar" style=3D"color: rgb(191, 199, 213); b=
ackground-color: rgb(41, 45, 62);"><code class=3D"codeBlockLines_p187"><spa=
n class=3D"token-line" style=3D"color: rgb(191, 199, 213);"><span class=3D"=
token plain">SBATCH --nodes=3D4</span><br></span><span class=3D"token-line"=
 style=3D"color: rgb(191, 199, 213);"><span class=3D"token plain" style=3D"=
display: inline-block;"></span><br></span><span class=3D"token-line" style=
=3D"color: rgb(191, 199, 213);"><span class=3D"token plain">SBATCH --ntasks=
-per-node=3D40</span><br></span></code></pre><div class=3D"buttonGroup_6DOT=
