<h2 class=3D"anchor anchorWithStickyNavbar_LWe7" id=3D"common-slurm-error-m=
essages">Common Slurm Error Messages<a href=3D"https://hyak.uw.edu/docs/com=
pute/scheduling-jobs#common-slurm-error-messages" class=3D"hash-link" aria-=
label=3D"Direct link to Common Slurm Error Messages" title=3D"Direct link t=
o Common Slurm Error Messages">=E2=80=8B</a></h2>
<ul>
<li><strong><code>slurmstepd: error: Exceeded job memory limit</code></stro=
ng>: your program uses more memory than you allotted during node creation a=
nd it has run out of memory.  Get a node with more memory and try again.</l=
i>
<li><strong><code>(ReqNodeNotAvail, UnavailableNodes:n[&lt;node numbers lis=
t&gt;]</code></strong>: your node will not expire (and might be running one=
 of your jobs) before the next scheduled maintenance day.  Either get a nod=
e with a shorter <code>--time</code> duration or wait until after the maint=
enance has been completed.</li>
<li><strong><code>Unable to allocate resources: Invalid account or account/=
partition combination specified</code></strong>: you used <code>-p &lt;grou=
p_name&gt; -A &lt;group_name&gt;</code> and you do not belong to that group=
.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class=3D"anchor anchorWithStickyNavbar_LWe7" id=3D"utility-commands">Ut=
ility Commands<a href=3D"https://hyak.uw.edu/docs/compute/scheduling-jobs#u=
tility-commands" class=3D"hash-link" aria-label=3D"Direct link to Utility C=
ommands" title=3D"Direct link to Utility Commands">=E2=80=8B</a></h2>
<p>With <code>&lt;net_id&gt;</code> as your UW NetID and <code>&lt;group_na=
me&gt;</code> as your Hyak group partition name, and <code>&lt;job_id&gt;</=
code> as an individual job ID:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href=3D"https://slurm.schedmd.com/sinfo.html" target=3D"_blank" rel=
=3D"noopener noreferrer"><strong><code>sinfo</code></strong></a> is used to=
 view information about <code>klone</code> nodes and partitions. Use <code>=
sinfo -p &lt;group_name&gt;</code> to view information about your group's p=
artition or allocation. Use <code>sinfo -s</code> to see a list of all part=
itions.</li>
<li><a href=3D"https://slurm.schedmd.com/squeue.html" target=3D"_blank" rel=
=3D"noopener noreferrer"><strong><code>squeue</code></strong></a> is used t=
o view information about jobs located in the scheduling queue.  Use <code>s=
queue -p &lt;group_name&gt;</code> to view information about your group's n=
odes.  Use <code>squeue -u &lt;net_id&gt;</code> to view your jobs.</li>
<li><a href=3D"https://slurm.schedmd.com/scancel.html" target=3D"_blank" re=
l=3D"noopener noreferrer"><strong><code>scancel</code></strong></a> is used=
 to cancel jobs.  Use <code>scancel &lt;job_id&gt;</code> to cancel a job w=
ith the given job ID, or use <code>scancel -u &lt;net_id&gt;</code> to canc=
el all of your jobs.</li>
<li><a href=3D"https://slurm.schedmd.com/sstat.html" target=3D"_blank" rel=
=3D"noopener noreferrer"><strong><code>sstat</code></strong></a> displays s=
tatus information of a running job pertaining to CPU, Task, Node, Resident =
Set Size (RSS), and Virtual Memory (VM) statistics.  Read the <a href=3D"ht=
tps://slurm.schedmd.com/sstat.html" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noref=
errer"><strong>man page</strong></a> for a comprehensive list of format opt=
ions.</li>
<li><a href=3D"https://slurm.schedmd.com/sacct.html" target=3D"_blank" rel=
=3D"noopener noreferrer"><strong><code>sacct</code></strong></a> displays i=
nformation about completed jobs.  Read the <a href=3D"https://slurm.schedmd=
.com/sacct.html" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer"><strong>man =
page</strong></a> for a comprehensive list of format options.</li>
<li><a href=3D"https://slurm.schedmd.com/sreport.html" target=3D"_blank" re=
l=3D"noopener noreferrer"><strong><code>sreport</code></strong></a> generat=
es reports about job usage and cluster utilization from Slurm accounting (<=
code>sacct</code>) data.  For example, to get historical usage the group <c=
ode>&lt;group_name&gt;</code> in March 2020, use <code>sreport cluster User=
UtilizationByAccount Start=3D2020-03-01 End=3D2020-03-31 Accounts=3D&lt;gro=
up_name&gt;</code>.</li>
</ul>
